   Wilson-Dirac b=0.4 : max |S h(k) S^+ - h(Rk)| = 4.44e-15
   naive Weyl t3=0.3  : max |S h(k) S^+ - h(Rk)| = 1.22e-15
2. discrete maps found as intertwiners of the b=0 law; parity of the added term:
   Wilson-Dirac, term gamma5 (b0): {'P': '-1 (odd) [solution-space dim 1]', 'T': '+1 (even) [solution-space dim 1]', 'C': '+1 (even) [solution-space dim 1]'}
   CPT parity of b-term = product of P,T,C parities
   naive Weyl, scalar term (t3 cos.cos.cos multiplies 1): {'P': None, 'T': '+1 (even) [solution-space dim 1]', 'C': None}
